Ky separates its specific options from the standard `fetch` options within the private `#fetch` method of the `Ky` class. This is done by calling the `findUnknownOptions` utility function.

### Separation Logic

1.  Before making the `fetch` call, the `Ky#fetch` method invokes `findUnknownOptions(this.#options)` to get an object containing only the options that should be passed to the underlying `fetch` function's `init` parameter (`source/core/Ky.ts:945`).
2.  The `findUnknownOptions` function iterates over all the options provided to the Ky instance (`source/utils/options.ts:10-14`).
3.  It filters out any option key that is a known Ky-specific option (checked against `kyOptionKeys`) or a standard `RequestInit` option (checked against `requestOptionsRegistry`) (`source/utils/options.ts:21`).
4.  Any option that is not in either of those registries is considered an "unknown" or "passthrough" option. These options are added to a new object (`source/utils/options.ts:22`).
5.  This new object, containing only the passthrough options, is then supplied as the `init` object to the `fetch` call (`source/core/Ky.ts:970-974`).

### Code Reference

The core filtering logic is in `findUnknownOptions`:

```typescript
// source/utils/options.ts:5-27
export const findUnknownOptions = (
	options: Record<string, unknown>,
): Record<string, unknown> => {
	const unknownOptions: Record<string, unknown> = {};

	for (const key in options) {
		// Skip inherited properties
		if (!Object.hasOwn(options, key)) {
			continue;
		}

		// Forward every non-standard, non-Ky option to fetch().
		// We intentionally do not check whether the key also exists on `Request`, because some runtimes
		// patch `Request.prototype` with fetch-only extensions. For example, Next.js adds `next`, and the
		// old `key in request` heuristic dropped it unless Ky kept a special-case allowlist.
		// Passing all non-standard keys makes that allowlist unnecessary and preserves future fetch extensions too.
		if (!(key in requestOptionsRegistry) && !(key in kyOptionKeys)) {
			unknownOptions[key] = options[key];
		}
	}

	return unknownOptions;
};
```

This function is called here:

