The `.json()` shortcut on the `ResponsePromise` modifies request headers and has specific behavior for empty response bodies.

### Headers

When the `.json()` shortcut is used, it sets the `Accept` request header to `application/json` unless an `Accept` header has already been specified in the options.

This is implemented in the `Ky.create` method where body-parsing shortcuts are attached to the response promise. The code checks if an `accept` header exists, and if not, sets it to the appropriate MIME type for JSON.

